      <abstract>
        <para>
          A &stig; (&stiga;) is a configuration standard that the &disa; (&disaa;) publishes for a
          specific product and version. &openscap; and the &ssg; check systems against such
          standards automatically and can remediate rules that fail. For &productname; 16, the
          &ssg; contains no &stiga; profile. Administrators can scan the system against the other
          hardening profiles instead and tailor these profiles to local requirements.
        </para>
        <para>
          <emphasis role="bold">Prerequisites</emphasis>
        </para>
        <itemizedlist>
          <listitem>
            <para>
              &productnameshort; 16 in standard mode
            </para>
          </listitem>
          <listitem>
            <para>
              A user account with &sudo; privileges
            </para>
          </listitem>
          <listitem>
            <para>
              A non-production system for testing remediation
            </para>
          </listitem>
        </itemizedlist>
      </abstract>
